{
  "scene_id": "scene02_computational_inversion",
  "video_title": "What Is Machine Learning?",
  "scene_title": "The Computational Inversion",
  "order": 2,
  "voice": {
    "language": "en-IN",
    "speaker": "priya",
    "model": "bulbul:v3"
  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s2_n1",
      "text": "To understand machine learning, we have to change how we think about software."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n2",
      "text": "In traditional programming, we give the computer rules and data, and it gives us an answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n3",
      "text": "So the flow is: Rules plus Data gives Answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n4",
      "text": "In machine learning, the setup changes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n5",
      "text": "We give the system data and the correct answers, and we ask it to learn the rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n6",
      "text": "So the flow becomes: Data plus Answers gives Rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n7",
      "text": "That is the key shift."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n8",
      "text": "We are no longer writing the logic directly. We are giving the machine examples and letting it find the pattern behind them."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n9",
      "text": "Think of it this way. In traditional programming, we explain the solution step by step. In machine learning, we show enough examples that the machine can infer the solution on its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_n10",
      "text": "That is the basic idea behind the field."
    }
  ],
